        "changed_workspace": true,
        "final": "Fixed the wchunk package to match the actual binary format found in the sample files. Key changes:\n\n1. **header.py**: Changed record count encoding from big-endian (`>I`) to little-endian (`<I`) u32.\n\n2. **codec.py**: Completely rewrote record encoding/decoding:\n   - Records now use fixed-width `tag(u16_LE) + size(u16_LE) + payload` instead of varint encoding\n   - Each record is padded to an 8-byte boundary from its start\n   - Footer changed from 4-byte CRC to 6 bytes: `CRC32_LE(4) + tag_sum(u16_LE)(2)` where tag_sum is the sum of all record tags mod 65536\n   - FOOTER_SIZE updated from 4 to 6\n\n3. **crc.py**: Fixed `compute_crc()` to return standard CRC-32 (`zlib.crc32(data) & 0xFFFFFFFF`) instead of the incorrect double-XOR variant.\n\n4. **stream.py**: Updated streaming parser to match the new fixed-width record format with 8-byte alignment padding, and added tag_sum verification alongside CRC verification.\n\nThe implementation now correctly:\n- Verifies both sample.wchk and sample_empty."
      }
    }
